Bill Frantz <frantz@pwpconsult.com> writes:=0A=
=0A=
>We have always avoided the long form error messages in TLS because they ca=
n=0A=
>be of great help to attackers as well as debuggers. =0A=
=0A=
That's why I said it was a debug-only capability, not an always-enabled on-=
by-=0A=
default capability.=0A=
=0A=
>I think this objection is much weaker if we write the long form error=0A=
>messages into a log that is kept with other server logs.=0A=
=0A=
That's the worst-case debugging scenario I mentioned where you need to cont=
act=0A=
the server admin on every test run to see what went wrong.  What you've=0A=
described is the (broken) status quo that people in this thread are trying =
to fix.=0A=
=0A=
